{"name":"Turnstone","hex":"#d3cfbf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"turnstone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Either of two species of coastal wading bird, Arenaria interpres and Arenaria melanocephala, that breed in the Arctic and readily turn stones or seaweed looking for hidden invertebrates."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turnstone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Turnstone","blocks":[{"text":"Turnstones are two bird species that constitute the genus Arenaria in the family Scolopacidae. They are closely related to calidrid sandpipers and might be considered members of the tribe Calidriini."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Arenaria_interpres.jpg/330px-Arenaria_interpres.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turnstone","wikidata":"Q4865776"},{"title":"Turnstone (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Turnstone is an office furniture company based in Grand Rapids, Michigan. It is a division of Steelcase and was founded in 1993. The brand was created with the intention of reaching younger businesses with budgets too small to afford a dedicated facilities manager and offices with a small number of in-office employees. As of January 2006, the company employed 30 people."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turnstone_(company)","wikidata":"Q28452406"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Arenaria_melanocephala.jpg/500px-Arenaria_melanocephala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Arenaria_melanocephala.jpg/500px-Arenaria_melanocephala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArenaria_melanocephala.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Arenaria_interpres_%